# FUSE third-party pin: AMD FidelityFX SDK, FSR1 (EASU + RCAS), CAS, FSR 3.1 upscaler and FSR 3.1 frame generation
# subset. Vendored verbatim, no local edits.
# Only the files listed below are vendored: the portable core headers (ffx_core*.h, ffx_common_types.h),
# the FSR1 and CAS GPU headers, the two host headers that declare the effect versions (kept for the pin;
# FUSE does not compile the FidelityFX host runtime), and the Vulkan GLSL pass entry points.
# FSR 3.1 upscaler (WP-4.2, added 2026-09-24, same tag / commit): the GPU headers the eight Vulkan passes
# include (gpu/fsr3upscaler/*.h minus the HLSL callbacks and the debug view), gpu/spd/ffx_spd.h (the luma and
# shading-change pyramids) and the eight GLSL pass entry points (prepare inputs, luma pyramid, shading-change
# pyramid, shading change, prepare reactivity, luma instability, accumulate, RCAS). Not vendored: the FSR 3.1
# host component (sdk/src/components/fsr3upscaler), the FidelityFX Vulkan backend, FidelityFX-SC, frame
# generation (WP-4.4) and anything FSR 4. The effect version is FFX_FSR3UPSCALER_VERSION 3.1.4
# (sdk/include/FidelityFX/host/ffx_fsr3upscaler.h, not vendored). FUSE compiles the passes with
# glslangValidator (Source/FUSE/Renderer/cmake/rp_wp42.cmake) and drives them from a clean-room host
# (Source/FUSE/Renderer/src/upscale_backends/fsr3/).
# FSR 3.1 frame generation (WP-4.4, added 2026-09-24, same tag / commit): the GPU headers of the optical-flow and
# frame-interpolation effects that their Vulkan passes include (gpu/opticalflow/*.h and gpu/frameinterpolation/*.h
# minus the HLSL callbacks and the debug view) and their Vulkan GLSL pass entry points (7 optical flow: prepare luma,
# luminance pyramid, SCD histogram, SCD divergence, search v5, filter v5, scale v5; 10 frame interpolation:
# reconstruct and dilate, setup, reconstruct previous depth, game motion vector field, game vector field
# inpainting pyramid, optical flow vector field, disocclusion mask, interpolation, inpainting pyramid,
# inpainting). Effect versions: FFX_OPTICALFLOW_VERSION 1.1.2 and FFX_FRAMEINTERPOLATION_VERSION 1.1.3
# (sdk/include/FidelityFX/host/ffx_{opticalflow,frameinterpolation}.h, not vendored). Not vendored: the host
# components (sdk/src/components/{opticalflow,frameinterpolation,fsr3}), the ffx-api frame-generation provider,
# the frame-interpolation swapchains, the debug-view pass and anything FSR 4. FUSE compiles the passes with
# glslangValidator (Source/FUSE/Renderer/cmake/rp_wp44.cmake) and drives them from a clean-room host
# (Source/FUSE/Renderer/src/framegen/).
# FUSE uses them two ways: the CPU single-source ports in
# Source/FUSE/Renderer/include/fuse/renderer/upscale/{fsr1,cas}_kernel.hpp transcribe the float32 paths, and the
# fuse_upscale_gpu_reference gate compiles shaders/vk/**.glsl with glslangValidator and runs them on
# Lavapipe to check the ports numerically.
# Checked by `fuse_lint vendored-pins` (ctest: fuse_lint_vendored_pins_fidelityfx).
# To update: re-fetch every file below from the new SDK tag (same paths under sdk/ and the repo root
# LICENSE.txt), then update version, tag, commit, header_version and every sha256 together. sha256 is
# over the file with CRLF normalized to LF.
